 and empirical review</article-title><source><italic>Psychological Bulletin</italic></source><year>1987</year><volume>101</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>5</fpage><lpage>27</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="B31"><label>31</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Erdelyi</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><name><surname>Becker</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hypermnesia for pictures: incremental memory for pictures but not words in multiple recall trials</article-title><source><italic>Cognitive Psychology</italic></source><year>1974</year><volume>6</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>159</fpage><lpage>171</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="B32"><label>32</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Barnier</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Hung</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Conway</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Retrieval-induced forgetting of emotional and unemotional autobiographical memories</article-title><source><italic>Cognition and Emotion</italic></source><year>2004</year><volume>18</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>457</fpage><lpage>477</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="B33"><label>33</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bluck</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Levine</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Laulhere</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Autobiographical remembering and hypermnesia: a comparison of older and younger adults</article-title><source><italic>Psychology and Aging</italic></source><year>1999</year><volume>14</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>671</fpage><lpage>682</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1063